------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY (web source reproduced)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Architecture: the web module-level pub/sub store (`openContextMenu`/`closeContextMenu`/
`subscribe`/`getSnapshot`, monotonic `nonce`, `restoreFocusEl`) + single portal host
(`ContextMenuRoot`/`ContextMenuView`) + `useContextMenu` hook are reproduced as:
  - ContextMenuStore (@MainActor @Observable, P1/S8 seam) injected via the environment +
    a process-wide `.shared` ("open from anywhere") — open() guards empty, bumps nonce,
    emits view.opened; close() restores trigger focus; invoke() closes then runs the action.
  - ContextMenuHost (the `ContextMenuRoot` peer) overlays a dismiss scrim + positioned panel.
  - contextMenuTrigger(_:) view modifier (the `useContextMenu` peer; named to avoid the
    pre-existing `tsContextMenu` system-menu modifier) — secondary press-and-hold + a
    VoiceOver action; imperative `store.open(_:at:)` mirrors the web imperative `openMenu`.
Data (web `ContextMenuItem`): id, label, icon(->SF Symbol systemImage), onClick(->@MainActor
  action), disabled, destructive, shortcut — reproduced verbatim (ContextMenuItem).
Behaviour contract (web): ArrowUp/Down skip disabled rows + wrap; Home/End jump first/last;
  Enter/Space invoke; Tab/Escape close; outside-tap/resize close; first ArrowDown -> first
  enabled; viewport-overflow flip (right->x, bottom->y, clamp to margin). The navigation walk
  and the measure-and-flip maths are extracted into the pure, unit-tested ContextMenuNavigation
  + ContextMenuLayout adapter (the "cached -> projection" seam).
i18n (P1/S10): the one web literal `t('contextMenu.menuLabel','Context menu')` plus the native
  VoiceOver chrome are all keys in the "ContextMenu" table (ContextMenu.strings); zero English
  literals in Swift. Accessibility: role=menu container label; each row is a button with label +
  destructive/disabled/shortcut hints; selected row carries .isSelected.
Telemetry (P1/S11): view.opened emitted with surface slug "ContextMenu" on each successful open.
charts/maps: NONE in the web source -> none added (no Swift Charts / MapKit needed).

States (honesty — NO fabricated states): ContextMenu is a STATELESS UI primitive; the web source
does NO async fetching (its only "data sources" are React primitives useSyncExternalStore /
useTranslation / useId / useLayoutEffect), so the generic loading/error/stale/offline data-states
DO NOT EXIST in the source and were NOT invented. The reproduced real branches — all rendered in
ContextMenu.Previews.swift and covered by ContextMenu.Tests.swift — are: closed (host renders
nothing), open (positioned menu), the empty guard (open([]) is a no-op — the web never shows an
empty "blank box"; a defensive friendly row exists as belt-and-braces), and the per-item
enabled / disabled / destructive / with-icon / with-shortcut variants, plus keyboard-nav,
viewport-flip, and focus-restore.

